---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Nav from '../components/Nav.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
import LeadClose from '../components/LeadClose.astro';
import { reviews, reviewHref } from '../data/reviews';
import { caseStudyHref } from '../data/case-studies';

const aiReview = reviews.find((r) => r.slug === 'ai-readiness-review')!;

const site = Astro.site ?? new URL('https://aragrow.me');
const pageUrl = new URL('/ai-consulting-and-automation/', site).href;

const structuredData = [
  {
    '@context': 'https://schema.org',
    '@type': 'Service',
    name: 'AI Consulting and Automation',
    serviceType: 'AI consulting and business process automation',
    url: pageUrl,
    description:
      'AI consulting and business process automation for small and mid-size businesses. Finds the few workflows where AI pays off, then builds only those.',
    areaServed: ['Minneapolis, MN', 'Minnesota', 'United States'],
    availableLanguage: ['en', 'es'],
    provider: {
      '@type': 'Organization',
      name: 'AraGrow LLC',
      url: site.href,
      address: {
        '@type': 'PostalAddress',
        addressLocality: 'Minneapolis',
        addressRegion: 'MN',
        addressCountry: 'US',
      },
    },
  },
];
---

<Layout
  title="AI Consultant and Business Automation, Minnesota | AraGrow"
  description="AI consulting and automation for small and mid-size businesses. I find the two or three places AI actually pays off, automate those business processes, and build nothing else."
  structuredData={structuredData}
>
  <Nav />
  <main class="aic-page">

    <!-- Header -->
    <div class="aic-header">
      <div class="container">
        <div class="section-label">AI consulting and automation</div>
        <h1 class="aic-title">
          AI consulting and automation for small and mid-size businesses
        </h1>
        <p class="aic-intro">
          You have been told to do something with AI. Nobody has shown you where it would pay off
          in your business. I find the two or three workflows where it actually would, automate
          those business processes, and leave the rest alone.
        </p>
        <div class="aic-header-actions">
          <a href="/contact" class="btn btn-primary">Book a 30-minute conversation</a>
          <a href={reviewHref(aiReview.slug)} class="aic-header-link">
            Or start with the AI Readiness Review ({aiReview.price})
          </a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="container aic-container">

      <!-- The problem -->
      <section class="aic-section" aria-labelledby="aic-advice">
        <h2 id="aic-advice">Most AI advice is written to sell you a tool</h2>
        <p>
          The pitch you are getting describes a product, not your business. It assumes your data is
          clean, your process is written down, and the task repeats often enough to pay back the
          build. Three assumptions, and in most companies I look at, at least one of them is wrong.
        </p>
        <p>
          That is expensive in a specific way. You buy licenses, somebody configures the tool, it
          works in the demo, and six weeks later your team has gone back to the spreadsheet. The
          money is gone and the process did not change.
        </p>
      </section>

      <!-- How I pick -->
      <section class="aic-section" aria-labelledby="aic-pick">
        <h2 id="aic-pick">Finding the two or three places AI actually helps</h2>
        <p>
          I walk your main workflows with the people who run them, then sort every candidate into
          one of three buckets.
        </p>
        <ul class="aic-list">
          <li>
            <strong>Worth doing with AI.</strong> The task involves language, judgment at scale, or
            messy inputs that rules cannot cover. Enough volume to pay for itself.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Plain automation solves it for less.</strong> A scheduled script or an
            integration between two systems you already pay for does the same job, cheaper, and
            with no model to monitor.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Not worth doing yet.</strong> The data is not reliable enough, the process
            changes too often, or the volume is too low. I say so rather than build it.
          </li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          That third bucket is usually the biggest, and it is the reason this work costs less than
          people expect. Most of the value comes from deciding what not to build.
        </p>
      </section>

      <!-- What automation looks like -->
      <section class="aic-section" aria-labelledby="aic-looks">
        <h2 id="aic-looks">What automating a business process looks like</h2>
        <p>
          Two examples from work I am doing now, one for a client and one on my own business.
        </p>
        <div class="aic-cards">
          <article class="aic-card">
            <h3>Calls that were turning into missed work</h3>
            <p>
              A vacation rental cleaning business where the owner fielded every inquiry,
              reschedule, and cleaner callout herself. Routine traffic was burying calls that
              could have become jobs, and every quote was built by hand. We mapped the workflows
              first, then started with one thing: answer the basic questions, give an instant
              estimate from the property details, and pass only serious prospects to her.
            </p>
            <a class="aic-card-link" href={caseStudyHref('ai-front-desk-cleaning')}>
              Read the AI front desk case study
            </a>
          </article>
          <article class="aic-card">
            <h3>Running my own site without a CMS</h3>
            <p>
              I test technology on my own business before I recommend it. This site used to run on
              WordPress with a caching layer and a firewall to manage problems the architecture
              created. It is now static files with no database and no login, and I manage content
              in plain language with AI instead of a CMS. That is the limit I found by doing it,
              not by reading about it.
            </p>
            <a class="aic-card-link" href={caseStudyHref('aragrow-astro-ai-cms')}>
              Read the AI content management case study
            </a>
          </article>
        </div>
        <p class="aic-note">
          I am also building WrapInsights, an AI-powered analytics platform for business owners who
          are not technical.
        </p>
      </section>

      <!-- Entry point -->
      <section class="aic-section aic-entry" aria-labelledby="aic-start">
        <h2 id="aic-start">Where to start</h2>
        <p>
          {aiReview.intro}
        </p>
        <p class="aic-entry-meta">
          <strong>{aiReview.name}</strong> · {aiReview.price} · {aiReview.scope}
        </p>
        <ul class="aic-list">
          {aiReview.deliverables.map((d) => <li>{d}</li>)}
        </ul>
        <a href={reviewHref(aiReview.slug)} class="aic-entry-link">
          See the full {aiReview.name}
        </a>
      </section>

      <!-- One FAQ for the whole site, so this points at its AI section -->
      <section class="aic-section" aria-labelledby="aic-faq">
        <h2 id="aic-faq">Questions I get asked</h2>
        <p>
          The AI questions people ask most, from where it fits to what it costs and whether your
          data is ready, are answered together with the rest of the site's questions.
        </p>
        <a href="/faq#ai" class="aic-entry-link">Read the AI questions on the FAQ</a>
      </section>

      <LeadClose
        title="Tell me where the time goes"
        body="Describe the work that eats your week. I will tell you whether AI is the right answer, whether plain automation is cheaper, or whether the honest answer is to leave it alone for now."
        links={[
          { text: `See the ${aiReview.name}`, href: reviewHref(aiReview.slug) },
          { text: 'Take the free self-assessment', href: '/self-assessment' },
        ]}
      />
    </div>
  </main>
  <Footer />
</Layout>

<style>
  /* ── Header ── */
  .aic-header {
    background: linear-gradient(160deg, #5a1010 0%, #4a0c0c 55%, #3b0a0a 100%);
    color: #fdf6f4;
    padding: 80px 0 60px;
  }
  .aic-header .section-label { color: #E8B931; }
  .aic-title {
    font-family: 'Space Grotesk', sans-serif;
    font-size: clamp(2rem, 4vw, 3rem);
    font-weight: 700; line-height: 1.15;
    color: #fdf6f4; margin: 12px 0 20px;
    max-width: 820px;
  }
  .aic-intro {
    font-size: 1.05rem; line-height: 1.7;
    color: rgba(253, 246, 244, 0.82);
    max-width: 660px;
  }
  .aic-header-actions {
    margin-top: 28px;
    display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; align-items: center; gap: 16px 20px;
  }
  .aic-header-link {
    color: #E8B931; font-size: 0.92rem;
    text-decoration: underline; text-underline-offset: 3px;
  }
  .aic-header-link:hover { color: #fdf6f4; }

  /* ── Body ── */
  .aic-container { padding-top: 56px; padding-bottom: 80px; }
  .aic-section { margin-bottom: 56px; max-width: 760px; }
  .aic-section h2 {
    font-family: 'Space Grotesk', sans-serif;
    font-size: clamp(1.4rem, 2.6vw, 1.9rem);
    font-weight: 700; line-height: 1.25;
    margin-bottom: 18px;
  }
  .aic-section > p {
    font-size: 1rem; line-height: 1.75;
    color: var(--muted); margin-bottom: 16px;
  }
  .aic-list {
    list-style: none; padding: 0;
    margin: 0 0 16px;
  }
  .aic-list li {
    position: relative; padding-left: 22px; margin-bottom: 12px;
    font-size: 1rem; line-height: 1.7; color: var(--muted);
  }
  .aic-list li::before {
    content: ''; position: absolute;
    left: 4px; top: 11px;
    width: 7px; height: 7px; border-radius: 50%;
    background: var(--teal, #E8B931);
  }
  .aic-list strong { color: var(--text); }
  .aic-note { font-size: 0.95rem; color: var(--muted); }

  /* ── Example cards ── */
  .aic-cards {
    display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
    gap: 20px; margin: 0 0 20px;
  }
  .aic-card {
    padding: 24px 22px;
    background: var(--card); border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 14px;
  }
  .aic-card h3 {
    font-family: 'Space Grotesk', sans-serif;
    font-size: 1.05rem; font-weight: 700; line-height: 1.3;
    margin-bottom: 10px;
  }
  .aic-card p {
    font-size: 0.94rem; line-height: 1.7;
    color: var(--muted); margin-bottom: 14px;
  }
  .aic-card-link, .aic-entry-link {
    font-size: 0.9rem; font-weight: 500;
    color: var(--teal-text);
    text-decoration: underline; text-underline-offset: 3px;
  }
  .aic-card-link:hover, .aic-entry-link:hover { color: var(--teal); }

  /* ── Entry point ── */
  .aic-entry {
    padding: 28px 26px;
    background: var(--card); border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 16px;
  }
  .aic-entry-meta {
    font-size: 0.95rem; color: var(--muted); margin-bottom: 16px;
  }
  .aic-entry-meta strong { color: var(--text); }

  @media (max-width: 768px) {
    .aic-cards { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
    .aic-entry { padding: 24px 20px; }
  }
</style>
